## target="_blank" / window.open

Leave `setSupportMultipleWindows(false)`. The WebView then loads
`window.open` / `target="_blank"` navigations in place, which is what a shell
wants, and no external Chrome tab is involved.

Do **not** enable multiple windows and answer `onCreateWindow` with the same
WebView as the transport — `transport.webView = view` throws
`IllegalArgumentException: Parent WebView cannot host its own popup window` and
takes the app down. It happened on the third page of the client's test site. If
a project genuinely needs popups, the transport has to be a *different*,
throwaway WebView whose first navigation is forwarded to the main one.

